# Author components

**Prerequisites:** [first component](/docs/tutorials/first-component/).
**You will do:** declare a component, call it, pass a body, and preview a fixture.
**Verify:** `rocci view FILE --component Name` shows the fixture.
**Next:** [Write markup](/docs/how-to/write-markup/) or
[Components reference](/docs/reference/language/components/).

Canonical source: [Styling.rocci](/examples/styling/source/Styling-rocci/).

## Declare and call

Names are PascalCase. Consecutive leading capitals (`HTMLShell`) are rejected;
write `HtmlShell`. A self-closing tag is a one-argument call. A paired tag
passes nested markup as the extra `Html` parameter — there is no magic
`children` field.

```rocci
@component Card = |{ title }, content|
    <section>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        {content}
    </section>

@component Page = |_|
    <Card title="Hello">
        <p>Body is Html, not a string.</p>
    </Card>
```

`??` field defaults are **experimental**. Omit the field at the call site;
lowering fills it. Do not treat defaults as a shipped Roc language feature.

Qualified calls use the imported module: `<Design.Button />` → `Design.button`.

## Fixtures

```rocci
@fixture{target: Card}
cardExample = { title: "Preview" }
```

`rocci view` and `rocci browse` consume fixtures. HTTP declarations are ignored
in `view`. Keep fixtures next to the component they target.

## Library layout

Put reusable widgets in `components/`. Keep page-private helpers in the same
`.rocci` module. `rocci browse components/` lists fixtures across a directory.

**Related:** [Tags](/docs/reference/language/tags/), [Fixtures](/docs/reference/language/fixtures/),
[pure components](/docs/concepts/pure-components/).
